WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们现在是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
我们正在为你们制作终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:29.020
Welcome, everybody, to the email surveillance episode of Office Ladies.
欢迎大家收听本期《办公室女士》，今天我们要聊的是“邮件监控”那一集。

9
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:29.840
Howdy!
大家好！

10
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.580
It is Season 2, Episode 9, written by Jen Salata, directed by Paul Feig.
这是第二季第九集，由简·萨拉塔编剧，保罗·费格执导。

11
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.660
And we have a special guest in the studio with us today.
今天演播室里有一位特别嘉宾。

12
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.180
He played Bill, one of the members of Michael Scott's improv class.
他饰演了比尔，迈克尔·斯科特即兴表演课的成员之一。

13
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.760
It is our friend, Kin Jong!
他就是我们的朋友，金·钟！

14
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.400
Hey, guys.
嘿，大家好。

15
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.920
Thank you so much for having me.
非常感谢邀请我来。

16
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.000
We are so excited you are here.
你能来我们太激动了。

17
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.680
You are our second in-studio gueSt.
你是我们第二位来到演播室的嘉宾。

18
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:52.320
Yes!
没错！

19
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.840
You and Creed Bratton, Kin.
金，你和克里德·布拉顿并列。

20
00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.820
That is privileged company.
那可是相当尊贵的行列。

21
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.540
So I'm very, very excited to be here.
所以我非常、非常高兴能来到这里。

22
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.780
So seriously, thank you.
真的，谢谢你们。

23
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:01.620
And congrats.
也恭喜你们。

24
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.680
Congrats on the success of your podcaSt.
恭喜你们的播客大获成功。

25
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.740
Yeah, so I listen to it, and it's awesome.
我一直在听，真的很棒。

26
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.280
So thank you for having me.
所以谢谢你们邀请我。

27
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:07.740
Thanks, Kin.
谢谢你，金。

28
00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.000
And this is Kin's day off.
而且今天还是金的休息日。

29
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.060
And I mean, you're a busy, busy person.
我是说，你可是个大忙人。

30
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:18.180
I can't even get into The Masked Singer and what it means to my children and how much we have to talk about it.
我甚至还没法跟你聊《蒙面歌王》对我孩子们意味着什么，以及我们得花多少时间讨论它。

31
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.120
That's a whole other subject.
那是另一个话题了。

32
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:19.380
Sure, sure.
当然，当然。

33
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.240
But you're a busy guy, and we appreciate you coming in on your day off.
但你是个大忙人，我们很感激你在休息日抽空过来。

34
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:22.680
Oh, no.
噢，没关系。

35
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:23.640
Thank you.
谢谢你们。

36
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.760
Before we get into this episode, you two have known each other for a very long time.
在进入本集内容之前，你们俩认识很久了吧。

37
00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.540
When did you guys become friends?
你们是什么时候成为朋友的？

38
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:30.340
You did a movie together.
你们一起拍过电影吗？

39
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.140
I think, really, Kin, what crystallized our friendship was your 40th birthday.
金，我觉得真正让我们的友谊升华的，是你四十岁的生日。

40
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.880
Was it your 40th birthday, Kin?
是你的四十岁生日吗，金？

41
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.840
It was my 40th birthday.
确实是我四十岁生日。

42
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.700
Your 40th birthday.
你的四十岁生日。

43
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.040
Okay.
好吧。

44
00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.980
He's twisting in his chair right now.
他现在在椅子上坐立不安呢。

45
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.140
He literally is about to fall out of his chair.
他简直快从椅子上掉下来了。

46
00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.320
I don't know this story.
我不知道这个故事。

47
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:43.880
Okay.
好吧。

48
00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.540
So, you know, Kin had done The Office, but we didn't work together that day.
你知道，金拍过《办公室》，但那天我们没在一起工作。

49
00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.960
Our paths never crossed.
我们的交集从未重叠。

50
00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:54.640
And then years later, we're on hiatus from The Office, and I am going to be playing this
后来过了几年，我们在《办公室》的拍摄间隙，我正要去演这个

51
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.760
role on a movie called Furry Vengeance.
出演了一部叫《毛骨悚然》的电影。

52
00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.200
Brooke Shields was in it.
波姬·小丝也参演了。

53
00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.180
Brendan Fraser.
还有布兰登·费舍。

54
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.320
I was such a huge Brendan Fraser fan.
我以前可是布兰登·费舍的超级粉丝。

55
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:01.700
Me too.
我也是。

56
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:02.480
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

57
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.000
We were filming in the middle of nowhere, Massachusetts.
我们当时在马萨诸塞州一个偏僻的地方拍戏。

58
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.320
Day one.
第一天。

59
00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.800
I think we were like two doors apart on our floor.
我想我们当时住在同一层楼，中间隔了两扇门。

60
00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:09.100
Yeah, I know.
对，我知道。

61
00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:09.780
We were on the table.
我们当时在桌子旁边。

62
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.280
I think we were across from each other.
我觉得我们当时是面对面坐着。

63
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.280
We were across the hall.
我们住在走廊对面。

64
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.560
We were across the hall at the Radisson.
我们住在雷迪森酒店走廊的两侧。

65
00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.080
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

66
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:14.220
This is so cute.
这太可爱了。

67
00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:14.920
I come out of my room.
我走出房间。

68
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.140
This is so cute.
这太可爱了。

69
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.580
Kin comes out, and I'm like, hey, you picked the Radisson too.
肯走出来，我就说，嘿，你也选了雷迪森酒店啊。

70
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.080
Yeah, we're the only two actors.
对，我们是仅有的两个演员。

71
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.280
Yeah, we're the only two actors in the Radisson with the crew.
没错，我们是雷迪森酒店里仅有的两个和剧组住在一起的演员。

72
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:22.540
Yeah.
是啊。

73
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.320
So we just would hang out all the time.
所以我们总是待在一起。

74
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.600
We were always in the shuttle together.
我们总是坐同一辆班车。

75
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.500
We became pretty fast friends right away.
我们很快就成了好朋友。

76
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.060
Very fast friends.
非常好的朋友。

77
00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:33.320
And that first week was Kin's 40th birthday, and here he is away from his family.
第一周正好是肯的40岁生日，他当时远离家人。

78
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.680
You're a little sad about it.
你当时有点难过吧。

79
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:34.840
Yeah.
是啊。

80
00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.400
And we didn't have a car because we were on location.
而且因为我们在外景地，我们没有车。

81
00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.640
We had the day off.
我们那天正好休息。

82
00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.240
Our day off happened to be his birthday together, him and I.
我们的休息日正好是他的生日，我们俩在一起。

83
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.400
I said, you know what?
我说，你知道吗？

84
00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:46.300
I'm going to take you out for your birthday.
我要带你去过生日。

85
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:52.060
And from the Radisson, there was a – we were sort of up on a hill, and you could see down
从雷迪森酒店出来，有一个——我们当时在山上，你可以往下看。

86
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.520
the hill, down a big, steep hill in this parking lot was a P.F.
山下，顺着一个又大又陡的坡下去，停车场里有一家P.F.

87
00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:57.180
Chang's.
Chang's餐厅。

88
00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.540
And I said, I said, Ken, I'm taking you to P.F.
我就说，肯，我要带你去P.F.

89
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.700
Chang's for your birthday.
Chang's过生日。

90
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:04.400
Amazing.
太棒了。

91
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.060
Not – wait, I don't know why we didn't want to get a cab, but we –
不是——等等，我不知道为什么我们不想打车，但我们——

92
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:07.500
I know why.
我知道为什么。

93
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.200
Why, why?
为什么，为什么？

94
00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:09.700
You walked it?
你们走过去的？

95
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.240
We walked it, and it wasn't like it was connected in the parking lot.
我们走过去的，而且那地方并不是直接连着停车场的。

96
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.540
At one point, we had to like crawl a little bit through a grassy median thing.
有一段路，我们还得爬过一片草地隔离带。

97
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:17.940
Remember?
记得吗？

98
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.220
It was like the parking lot was separated by like a little bit of a grassy knoll.
停车场中间隔着一个小草丘。

99
00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.480
Anyway, we walked down this parking lot.
总之，我们走过了那个停车场。

100
00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.480
We go into P.F.
我们走进了P.F.

101
00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.860
Chang's at like 11 a.m.
大概是上午11点在Chang's餐厅。

102
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:31.660
There's no – there's like no one there.
那里根本……那里几乎没人。

103
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.020
We're the first people there.
我们是第一批到的。

104
00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:37.700
We ate so much and drank a ton of beer, and we were both really buzzed.
我们吃了很多，喝了一大堆啤酒，两人都喝得有点上头了。

105
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:37.860
Yep.
没错。

106
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.700
And now we have to walk up this hill, and we're like tipsy, and we're like, oh, my God,
现在我们得走上这个山坡，我们都有点醉醺醺的，我们就在想，天哪，

107
00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.480
this hill sucks on the way back.
回程走这个坡真是糟透了。

108
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.820
And Ken was like, what did you do to me?
Ken就说，你对我做了什么？

109
00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:56.240
Okay, what – you just decided mid-walk like, hey, I should just exercise.
好吧，你当时……你就在走路的时候突然决定，嘿，我该锻炼一下了。

110
00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:56.740
Yeah.
是啊。

111
00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.480
And you're like walking around the parking lot like you're doing laps.
然后你就绕着停车场走，就像在跑圈一样。

112
00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.880
I said, pump your arms, Ken.
我说，Ken，摆动你的手臂。

113
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:05.940
And then we're literally speed walking drunk at a Radisson parking lot.
然后我们就在Radisson酒店的停车场里，醉醺醺地竞走。

114
00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:06.940
Just remember, you're just –
记住，你只是……

115
00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.300
I was like, Ken, pump your arMs.
我当时说，Ken，摆动你的手臂。

116
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.260
Come on, pump your arMs.
来吧，摆动你的手臂。

117
00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.140
We're going to get a workout.
我们要锻炼一下。

118
00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.980
And I was just crying laughing.
我当时笑得眼泪都出来了。

119
00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.380
You were crying laughing so hard.
你当时笑得太厉害了，眼泪都出来了。

120
00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.060
You were like, what are we doing?
你当时说，我们到底在干什么？

121
00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.440
And you turned to me –
然后你转向我——

122
00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.620
Pump, pump, pump.
摆动，摆动，摆动。

123
00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.880
Okay, I'm taking us off topic.
好吧，我把话题扯远了。

124
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.060
All right, focus.
好了，集中注意力。

125
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.360
Jenna, how about a summary?
Jenna，来个总结怎么样？

126
00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:29.760
In this episode, Michael gains access to everyone's emails and discovers that Jim is hosting a barbecue.
在这一集中，Michael获得了查看所有人邮件的权限，发现Jim正在举办烧烤派对。

127
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.960
Everyone except Michael has been invited.
除了Michael，所有人都收到了邀请。

128
00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.680
Michael fumes, but Jim holds firm.
Michael气炸了，但Jim坚持不松口。

129
00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.180
After attending his weekly improvisation class, Michael crashes the barbecue after all,
在参加完每周的即兴表演课后，Michael还是闯入了烧烤派对，

130
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.960
and Pam suspects Dwight and Angela might be a couple.
而且Pam怀疑Dwight和Angela可能是一对。

131
00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:48.880
Dun, dun, dun.
当当当。

132
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.660
Yes, this is a big episode.
没错，这是重要的一集。

133
00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.740
This is a big episode.
这是重要的一集。

134
00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.600
All right, fast fact number one.
好了，快速事实第一条。

135
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.240
We always start with fast facts, Ken.
我们总是从快速事实开始，Ken。

136
00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.900
Well, Jenna loves a fast fact.
嗯，Jenna喜欢快速事实。

137
00:04:59.000 --> 00:04:59.180
Okay.
好吧。

138
00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.000
Okay, so don't mess with them.
所以别搞砸了。

139
00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.420
You like my fast facts?
你喜欢我的快速事实吗？

140
00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:07.700
I like them too, but it's like you coined the phrase fast fact.
我也喜欢，但感觉“快速事实”这个词是你发明的。

141
00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.580
Did I not?
难道不是吗？

142
00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:09.260
Ah!
啊！

143
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:10.960
Did I not?
难道不是吗？

144
00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.600
Oh, Joel McHill's flipping you off.
哦，Joel McHill在对你竖中指。

145
00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:13.220
Bad Joel.
坏Joel。

146
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.940
Do our listeners need some context?
我们的听众需要背景信息吗？

147
00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:15.580
Bad Joel.
坏Joel。

148
00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.420
This is Joel McHill, my nemesis on community.
这是Joel McHill，我在《废柴联盟》里的宿敌。

149
00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:23.540
So we are in one recording booth, and the glass window is facing his.
我们现在在一个录音棚里，玻璃窗正对着他的录音棚。

150
00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:30.800
We can see him through the glass, and he can see us, and he is being offensive and aggressive.
我们可以透过玻璃看到他，他也能看到我们，他现在表现得很无礼且具有攻击性。

151
00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.020
He gave us the bird, and then he mooned us.
他向我们竖了中指，然后又脱下裤子露屁股羞辱我们。

152
00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.160
Now he's coming in.
他现在进来了。

153
00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.300
This is, no, lock it.
这是，不，锁上它。

154
00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:36.860
Now he's coming in.
他现在进来了。

155
00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:37.680
Lock it.
锁上它。

156
00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.440
I am here with friends, all right?
我是和朋友们一起来的，好吗？

157
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.040
You can have my microphone.
你可以用我的麦克风。

158
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.220
I'm here with people who I love and adore.
我和我爱戴的人在一起。

159
00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.640
Guys, my favorite Parks and Rec episode.
伙计们，这是我最喜欢的《公园与游憩》剧集。

160
00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.520
This is the office, Joel.
乔尔，这是《办公室》的片场。

161
00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.560
Where Chris Pratt.
克里斯·帕拉特在哪？

162
00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.300
No, this is the office.
不，这是《办公室》的片场。

163
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.200
How dare you?
你怎么敢这样？

164
00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.820
This is the show that started it all.
这是开启一切的剧集。

165
00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:59.100
And as much as Angela and Jenna are best friends, you and I, if we had a show, we would call ourselves
尽管安吉拉和珍娜是最好的朋友，但你和我，如果我们有档节目，我们会称自己为

166
00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.200
community enemies.
社区公敌。

167
00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.820
Because I didn't like you.
因为我以前不喜欢你。

168
00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.800
I never liked you for six seasons.
我有六季的时间都不喜欢你。

169
00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.620
I was over a hundred episodes.
我拍了一百多集呢。

170
00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:08.100
We barely tolerated each other.
我们当时几乎无法忍受对方。

171
00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:12.580
And the antipathy has only grown in the last four years.
而且这种反感在过去四年里有增无减。

172
00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:13.720
That is true.
那是真的。

173
00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.740
And here's the thing.
关键是这样。

174
00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.860
When we saved Ken's career.
当我们拯救了肯的职业生涯时。

175
00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.060
