别再提拯救我职业生涯的事了。

176
00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:20.740
Stop it.
住口。

177
00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.780
Have you ever listened?
你听过吗？

178
00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:22.380
Stop it.
住口。

179
00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.460
Has he talked about how many?
他有提过多少次吗？

180
00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:24.260
Just knock it off.
别再说了。

181
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.620
When you look at his.
当你看看他的。

182
00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:26.240
Knock it off.
别再说了。

183
00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.500
When you look at his filmography.
当你看看他的电影作品集时。

184
00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:28.440
Stop it.
住口。

185
00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.000
Hangover.
《宿醉》。

186
00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:29.740
Stop it.
住口。

187
00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:30.540
Hangover 2.
《宿醉2》。

188
00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:31.160
How dare you?
你怎么敢这样？

189
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.480
Hangover 3.
《宿醉3》。

190
00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.140
How dare you?
你怎么敢这样？

191
00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.660
I'm sorry, but you're leaving furry vengeance.
抱歉，但你把《毛茸茸的复仇》给漏了。

192
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.600
That was a movie Angela and I did.
那是安吉拉和我一起拍的电影。

193
00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.380
Together, right before community.
就在《废柴联盟》之前。

194
00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.320
I can't believe you're saying this on mic.
真不敢相信你对着麦克风说这些。

195
00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.920
Look, I'm here as a humble day player.
听着，我只是作为一个卑微的临时演员来的。

196
00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:47.580
Talking about how I was Bill on email surveillance.
聊聊我在《电子邮件监控》里演比尔的事。

197
00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:55.920
I want to go on record and say, I really think community enemies is a great podcaSt.
我想郑重声明，我真的觉得《社区公敌》是个很棒的播客。

198
00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:56.960
I'd be a good companion.
我会是个很好的搭档。

199
00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:57.800
That just happened.
刚才发生了什么。

200
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.760
Will you please do a rewatch of community with Joel and call it community enemies.
你愿意和乔尔一起重温《废柴联盟》并把它命名为《社区公敌》吗？

201
00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.720
And just give each other s**t for like an hour.
然后互相损上个把小时。

202
00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:08.200
That is.
确实如此。

203
00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.260
Speaking of, I'm a really big fan of community.
说到这个，我可是《废柴联盟》的超级粉丝。

204
00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:15.880
And I remembered that we would meet up at all the NBC events.
我记得我们以前在NBC的各种活动上都会碰面。

205
00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.640
Because we were on air at the same time.
因为我们当时是在同一时期播出的。

206
00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.500
And you had such a funny group of people.
你们那部剧里有一群特别逗的人。

207
00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.200
And I loved the show.
我非常喜欢那部剧。

208
00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.220
And I would be interested in hearing some behind the scenes banter about that.
我很想听听关于那部剧的幕后趣事。

209
00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.880
Yeah, no, it was huge.
是啊，没错，那部剧太火了。

210
00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:36.020
Because I think the premiere, I think the first two episodes, I think we followed The Office just to survive on the air on NBC.
因为我觉得首播的时候，前两集，我们应该是紧接着《办公室》播出的，才得以在NBC存活下来。

211
00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:40.800
Because, I mean, The Office, you know, Thursday nights NBC was the flagship show.
毕竟，《办公室》可是当时NBC周四晚间的王牌节目。

212
00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:49.380
And so when we found out that it would air after The Office, we were always, you know, that was like the anchor for us.
所以当我们得知要在《办公室》之后播出时，我们一直觉得，那就是我们的救命稻草。

213
00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:55.600
And it's funny how you think certain shows like The Office has helped other shows.
很有意思的是，你会发现像《办公室》这样的剧集确实帮到了其他剧。

214
00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:03.620
And then, you know, get on the air, stay on the air, and then give actors like myself and unfortunately Joel, you know, a career.
让我们得以播出、留存，还给了像我这样，以及不幸的是，给了乔尔这样的演员一份事业。

215
00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:10.360
And that's been, you know, I'm grateful for mine, you know, but the fans should be regretting Joel.
我很感激我自己的这份事业，但粉丝们应该为乔尔感到遗憾。

216
00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:11.540
I'm looking at Joel.
我正看着乔尔呢。

217
00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.700
And you can quote me on that.
你可以把这话引用出去。

218
00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:15.580
We will.
我们会引用的。

219
00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:16.260
We will.
我们一定会引用的。

220
00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:21.700
We're going to use that as our promo clip for this episode.
我们要把它剪进这期节目的宣传片里。

221
00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:22.220
Yes.
没错。

222
00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.140
All right.
好吧。

223
00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.460
So before we were so rudely interrupted.
那么，在我们被粗鲁地打断之前。

224
00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:26.060
I know.
我知道。

225
00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.060
Before Joel McHale came in, and he trashed our desk.
在乔尔·麦克哈尔进来把我们的桌子搞得乱七八糟之前。

226
00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:30.160
He literally trashed.
他真的是把桌子搞乱了。

227
00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.880
He dumped over a cup of pens.
他把笔筒都倒了。

228
00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:35.340
He moved our coffee and our tea.
他还挪动了我们的咖啡和茶。

229
00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:36.040
I know.
我知道。

230
00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.340
I was going to discuss my fast facts.
我本来要讲我的快问快答环节。

231
00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:38.760
Yes.
没错。

232
00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.900
Fast fact number one.
快问快答第一条。

233
00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:44.760
This is the first episode from writer Jen Salata.
这是编剧简·萨拉塔创作的第一集。

234
00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:46.320
I love Jen Salata.
我超爱简·萨拉塔。

235
00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:52.140
Now, she will go on to write fan favorites such as Beach Games and Benihana Christmas and many more.
后来她还创作了像《海滩游戏》和《本尼哈纳圣诞节》等深受粉丝喜爱的剧集，还有很多其他作品。

236
00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:59.380
She also directed several episodes, but this was her first episode as a writer, and we love Jen.
她还执导过几集，但这集是她作为编剧的第一集，我们都很爱简。

237
00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:05.560
One of my favorite memories of Jen, I think more than any other writer, is she would giggle behind the monitor.
关于简，我最喜欢的记忆之一，我觉得比其他任何编剧都深刻，就是她总会在监视器后面咯咯笑。

238
00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:06.260
She would get so tickled.
她总是很容易被逗乐。

239
00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.040
And her shoulders would shake.
肩膀还会跟着抖动。

240
00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.260
It's not that it was easy to make her laugh.
并不是说她很容易被取悦。

241
00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.980
It was that she was ready to laugh.
而是她随时准备着大笑。

242
00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.320
She was ready to love what you were doing.
她随时准备着去欣赏你的表演。

243
00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.200
Mindy was like that, too, I have to say.
我得说，敏迪也是这样。

244
00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.100
I just loved her energy on set.
我特别喜欢她在片场的那种活力。

245
00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.020
I think that helps with the actors, right?
我觉得这对演员很有帮助，对吧？

246
00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.420
Like, just give the performers the talent more confidence, you know?
就像是，给表演者和天才们更多自信，你懂吗？

247
00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:31.320
And Jen is the type of person, because she's so earnest and sincere, that when she does laugh, it's like her whole body gives into it.
简就是那种人，因为她非常真诚、纯粹，所以当她大笑时，整个人都会沉浸其中。

248
00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.100
It's just a sweet, wonderful thing to witness.
那真是一件既甜蜜又美妙的事情。

249
00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:35.700
It really is.
确实如此。

250
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:36.400
It really is.
确实如此。

251
00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:37.540
All right.
好吧。

252
00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.640
Fast fact number two.
第二个快讯。

253
00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:39.560
Do it.
开始吧。

254
00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:41.520
See, they're fast, and they're faSt.
你看，他们既快，又“快”。

255
00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:42.020
Oh, my God.
天哪。

256
00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.640
I'm like slow lie Joe McHale.
我就像个慢吞吞的乔·麦克海尔。

257
00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:44.380
That's right.
没错。

258
00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:48.180
All right, we have two big guest stars for this episode.
好了，我们这集有两位重量级客串明星。

259
00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:53.160
The first is Omivadia, who plays the IT specialist, Sadiq.
第一位是奥米瓦迪亚，他饰演IT专家萨迪克。

260
00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:58.160
Now, he is also the star of this Bollywood movie called Three Idiots.
他还是宝莱坞电影《三傻大闹宝莱坞》的主演。

261
00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.580
It was a huge smash hit.
那部电影非常火爆。

262
00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:05.380
Like, he's just a gigantic star from this movie.
他就是因为那部电影而成了超级巨星。

263
00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.860
And then he was also in our episode.
后来他也参与了我们这一集的拍摄。

264
00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:12.960
And our other guest star, Ken Jeong, who is in the room with us now.
另一位客串明星是郑肯，他现在就在我们房间里。

265
00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:17.260
Well, Ken, I did not know you when you got the part on The Office.
肯，你拿到《办公室》那个角色的时候，我还不认识你。

266
00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.220
We met years later.
我们是多年后才认识的。

267
00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:18.500
Right, right.
对，没错。

268
00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.740
Can you tell us a little bit about how you got the part?
你能跟我们说说你是怎么拿到那个角色的吗？

269
00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.440
I used to be a doctor.
我以前是个医生。

270
00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:23.520
I used to be a physician.
我以前是名内科医生。

271
00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:29.540
But I really, I was auditioning just like during, like after work or during lunch.
但我当时真的就是在下班后或者午休时去试镜。

272
00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:36.960
And then Allison Jones just took a liking to me, and she got me an audition for The Office.
后来艾莉森·琼斯看中了我就推荐我去试镜《办公室》。

273
00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:42.360
And it was, keep in mind, I really had no screen credits, but she brought me straight into Producers.
你要知道，我当时几乎没有任何影视作品，但她直接带我去了制片人面试。

274
00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.420
I still remember it vividly.
我至今记忆犹新。

275
00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:52.380
It was in 05, and I had read in front of Jen Salata and Paul Feig, the director of the episode.
那是05年，我在珍·萨拉塔和该集导演保罗·费格面前读了剧本。

276
00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.340
And I was a huge fan of Paul's from Freaks and Geeks.
我是保罗执导的《怪胎与书呆》的超级粉丝。

277
00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.400
So I was already just geeking out in The Office.
所以我当时在《办公室》剧组就已经激动得不行了。

278
00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:02.760
And I'm not saying it because you're my friends and because this is The Office, ladies.
女士们，我这么说可不是因为你们是我的朋友，也不是因为这是《办公室》。

279
00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:07.460
It was my favorite show on TV, and I'm just a huge BBC office fan.
它是我电视上最喜欢的节目，我还是BBC版《办公室》的铁粉。

280
00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.360
So I just knew the show inside out.
所以我对这部剧了如指掌。

281
00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:17.700
And so it was really one of the first times, maybe the first time ever, I was brought in for a producer's read with the director in the room.
那真的是我第一次，甚至可能是唯一一次，在导演在场的情况下参加制片人面试。

282
00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:29.620
And it's funny now because a lot of people, and rightly so, attribute my acting as very over the top and very, like on community, very, very, just pushing it out.
现在回想起来很有趣，因为很多人——而且说得没错——认为我的表演风格非常夸张，就像在《废柴联盟》里那样，非常非常用力。

283
00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:39.880
And it's very, you know, very ironic, like really, I think my breakthrough role was playing something very understated and with just maybe two lines.
这真的很讽刺，因为我觉得我的成名作其实是那种非常内敛、可能只有两句台词的角色。

284
00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.920
And I would basically whisper every line, and I improvised a look to camera, even if it wasn't scripted.
我基本上是低声说出每一句台词，而且我还即兴加了一个看向镜头的动作，尽管剧本里并没有写。

285
00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:46.360
Nice!
太棒了！

286
00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:52.440
And I remember, I still remember where I go, like, he told me he couldn't say, but he has a gun.
我记得，我依然记得当时的情景，他说他不能说出来，但他有枪。

287
00:11:52.580 --> 00:12:00.960
And I just looked straight down the barrel, and Paul, Feig, and Jen laughed so hard at this tiny movement.
我就直勾勾地盯着枪口，保罗·费格和珍被我这个小动作逗得大笑不止。

288
00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:01.800
That little choice.
那个小小的选择。

289
00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:02.700
That little choice.
那个小小的选择。

290
00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:06.000
And I still remember, like, Paul could not stop laughing.
我依然记得，保罗当时笑得停不下来。

291
00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.720
And whenever I see Paul, we still talk about it.
每次见到保罗，我们还会聊起这件事。

292
00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:21.600
And it's still, it's one of those things in an actor's life where sometimes, like, I've forgotten years of working on community, probably because of Joel.
这依然是演员生涯中那种特别的时刻，有时候，比如我在《废柴联盟》工作多年的记忆都模糊了，可能是因为乔尔的原因。

293
00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:28.240
And, but I remember every single minute of my maybe three hours on the office.
但我依然记得我在《办公室》那三个小时里的每一分钟。

294
00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:34.780
You know, it's just really, it's one of those things, and I'm sure you have that too in your careers of, you just remember your first time.
你知道，这真的很特别，我相信你们在各自的职业生涯中也有这种感觉，就是你会永远记得第一次。

295
00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:39.800
And you just know, if it's not a watershed event, it's maybe your favorite event.
如果你不觉得这是个转折点，那它至少也是你最难忘的经历。

296
00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.460
And that's kind of what, what the office means to me, yeah.
这就是《办公室》对我而言的意义，没错。

297
00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:44.560
Oh, I love that.
噢，我太喜欢这个故事了。

298
00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:44.820
Wow.
哇。

299
00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.640
That's such a wonderful thing to share.
这真是太美妙的分享了。

300
00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:47.920
I love that, Ken.
我喜欢这个，肯。

301
00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:48.380
Thank you.
谢谢。

302
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:48.620
Very grateful.
非常感激。

303
00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:53.480
Well, I have some fan questions, if you don't mind, answering, about your time in the scene.
好的，如果你不介意的话，我有一些粉丝关于你当时在那个场景里的提问。

304
00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.400
Jason P.
杰森·P。

305
00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.960
asked, once you started shooting the scenes, how much of the improv was actually improv?
问到，一旦你们开始拍摄那些场景，有多少即兴表演是真的即兴发挥的？

306
00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.280
That's a great question.
这是个好问题。

307
00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:08.080
