这些，伙计们，德怀特可是深思熟虑过的。

614
00:26:43.770 --> 00:26:46.590
This is what could happen, and he'd have to do an immediate takeover.
这就是可能发生的情况，而他必须立即接管。

615
00:26:46.850 --> 00:26:47.670
Immediate takeover.
立即接管。

616
00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:51.410
And Michael has that great line where he says, you know what, Dwight?
迈克尔有句很棒的台词，他说，你知道吗，德怀特？

617
00:26:51.590 --> 00:26:56.090
If I step on a mine in Scranton, Pennsylvania, you can have my job.
如果我在宾夕法尼亚州的斯克兰顿踩到地雷，我的职位就归你了。

618
00:26:56.310 --> 00:26:57.510
He's so annoyed.
他当时烦透了。

619
00:26:57.670 --> 00:26:57.850
Yeah.
确实。

620
00:26:58.170 --> 00:27:05.030
So the next big scene is kind of in the bullpen when Oscar confronts Michael about spying on
下一个大场面是在办公区，奥斯卡质问迈克尔为什么要监视

621
00:27:05.030 --> 00:27:05.710
everyone's emails.
每个人的邮件。

622
00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:07.170
He does it in front of everyone.
他当着所有人的面这么做了。

623
00:27:07.370 --> 00:27:11.290
I loved it whenever Oscar confronted Michael in front of everyone, and he does this throughout
我一直很喜欢奥斯卡当众质问迈克尔的戏份，他在整部剧里都这么做，

624
00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:14.910
the series, and it's just some of my favorite moments of the show.
这绝对是我最喜欢的剧集片段之一。

625
00:27:14.910 --> 00:27:17.730
He is able to take Michael to task like no one else.
他能像其他人一样去指责迈克尔。

626
00:27:17.830 --> 00:27:22.350
I think Stanley also does this from time to time, but Stanley is usually more under his
我觉得斯坦利偶尔也会这样，但斯坦利通常更倾向于

627
00:27:22.350 --> 00:27:23.010
breath, right?
小声嘀咕，对吧？

628
00:27:23.190 --> 00:27:25.910
Like, he's a little more to the side about it.
就像是，他对此表现得更隐晦一点。

629
00:27:26.090 --> 00:27:26.230
Yeah.
没错。

630
00:27:26.370 --> 00:27:30.350
In this scene, Steve does this never-ending robot bit.
在这一幕里，史蒂夫一直在做那个没完没了的机器人动作。

631
00:27:31.230 --> 00:27:36.110
Oscar's trying to get a word out, and Steve just keeps doing the robot thing.
奥斯卡想插话，但史蒂夫一直不停地做着机器人动作。

632
00:27:36.510 --> 00:27:37.890
I remember shooting that.
我记得拍摄那场戏的时候。

633
00:27:38.050 --> 00:27:41.310
So in the script, that was not supposed to go on for that long.
剧本里本来没打算让他演那么久的。

634
00:27:41.310 --> 00:27:45.510
That was supposed to just be like a quick little thing, but Steve really dragged it
那本该只是个小插曲，但史蒂夫把它拖得太长了，

635
00:27:45.510 --> 00:27:51.030
out, and that was an example, I think, of some of his just brilliant comedic timing.
我认为这就是他绝佳喜剧节奏感的一个例子。

636
00:27:51.310 --> 00:27:56.010
I honestly think that Steve would drag things out like that to see when he could get all
我真心觉得史蒂夫会故意把事情拖得那么长，就是为了看什么时候

637
00:27:56.010 --> 00:27:56.650
of us to break.
能让我们所有人都笑场。

638
00:27:56.870 --> 00:27:57.750
And we would break.
而我们确实笑场了。

639
00:27:57.790 --> 00:27:58.770
We did break in that.
我们在那场戏里确实笑场了。

640
00:27:58.970 --> 00:28:00.710
He was a little sadistic that way.
他在那方面确实有点小小的施虐倾向。

641
00:28:00.830 --> 00:28:02.330
He'd be like, oh, you haven't broken yet?
他会想，哦，还没笑场吗？

642
00:28:02.490 --> 00:28:03.390
How about this?
那这样呢？

643
00:28:03.470 --> 00:28:03.670
Yeah.
没错。

644
00:28:03.770 --> 00:28:04.410
How about this?
那这样呢？

645
00:28:04.630 --> 00:28:05.810
Kinsey, I see you going.
金西，我看到你快憋不住了。

646
00:28:06.150 --> 00:28:08.610
Like, he'd just keep going until we fell apart.
他会一直演下去，直到我们彻底崩溃笑场。

647
00:28:08.610 --> 00:28:13.230
Well, right after this, then, we have the little aside.
好吧，紧接着，我们有一个小小的旁白。

648
00:28:13.470 --> 00:28:15.410
Well, the erasing begins, right?
嗯，删除工作开始了，对吧？

649
00:28:15.550 --> 00:28:16.550
The erasing begins.
删除工作开始了。

650
00:28:16.810 --> 00:28:23.190
And Dwight says to Angela, if you have any sensitive emails, they need to be deleted immediately.
德怀特对安吉拉说，如果你有任何敏感邮件，必须立即删除。

651
00:28:24.030 --> 00:28:25.070
Pam overhears.
帕姆听到了。

652
00:28:25.430 --> 00:28:26.650
She calls Jim over.
她把吉姆叫了过来。

653
00:28:26.850 --> 00:28:28.650
She suspects that they might be a couple.
她怀疑他们可能是一对。

654
00:28:29.410 --> 00:28:35.670
This is the first moment where we call out that Dwight and Angela might be together.
这是我们第一次指出德怀特和安吉拉可能在一起的时刻。

655
00:28:35.670 --> 00:28:40.050
Well, the first moment that anyone in the office has any idea, right?
嗯，这是办公室里任何人第一次察觉到，对吧？

656
00:28:40.210 --> 00:28:40.510
Yes.
是的。

657
00:28:40.690 --> 00:28:40.810
Yeah.
没错。

658
00:28:41.630 --> 00:28:44.250
Fan question from Kelsey McGrath.
来自凯尔西·麦格拉思的粉丝提问。

659
00:28:44.570 --> 00:28:48.990
Angela, when did Angela and Rain find out that they were love interests?
安吉拉，安吉拉和雷恩是什么时候发现他们是恋爱关系的？

660
00:28:49.570 --> 00:28:54.770
I mean, I'm not sure if Rain had any heads up before I did, but I found out at the table read.
我是说，我不确定雷恩是否比我先知道，但我是在剧本围读会上发现的。

661
00:28:55.350 --> 00:28:55.830
Really?
真的吗？

662
00:28:56.090 --> 00:28:56.330
Yeah.
是的。

663
00:28:56.470 --> 00:28:59.230
When we sat down to read the script, and Oscar—
当我们坐下来读剧本时，奥斯卡——

664
00:28:59.230 --> 00:29:00.330
So no one warned you beforehand?
所以之前没有人提醒过你？

665
00:29:00.370 --> 00:29:01.850
No one warned me beforehand.
之前没有人提醒过我。

666
00:29:01.850 --> 00:29:02.910
I had no idea.
我完全不知情。

667
00:29:02.910 --> 00:29:08.090
And when we sat down at the table read, and we read that their Birkenstocks were bumping,
当我们坐下来围读剧本，读到他们的勃肯鞋碰到一起时，

668
00:29:08.690 --> 00:29:08.740
right?
对吧？

669
00:29:09.050 --> 00:29:09.950
I was like,
我当时就想，

670
00:29:10.430 --> 00:29:10.610
ha!
哈！

671
00:29:11.430 --> 00:29:11.770
What?
什么？

672
00:29:12.770 --> 00:29:16.270
Well, I remember there was an audible gasp in the room when we read that.
嗯，我记得当时读到那一段时，房间里传出了一阵惊呼声。

673
00:29:16.410 --> 00:29:21.330
There were times when we would do these table reads where people would be legitimately surprised
我们进行这些剧本围读时，有时大家确实会因为剧情反转而感到惊讶，

674
00:29:21.330 --> 00:29:24.010
by plot twists, and this was definitely one of them.
而这绝对是其中之一。

675
00:29:24.110 --> 00:29:26.170
This, when we found out Oscar was gay?
这个，还有我们发现奥斯卡是同性恋的时候？

676
00:29:26.310 --> 00:29:26.730
Yes.
是的。

677
00:29:26.910 --> 00:29:27.150
Right?
对吧？

678
00:29:27.310 --> 00:29:27.610
Yes.
是的。

679
00:29:27.610 --> 00:29:30.130
I mean, when we found out Jim and Pam were going to have a baby.
我是说，还有我们发现吉姆和帕姆要生孩子的时候。

680
00:29:30.290 --> 00:29:30.650
Yes!
没错！

681
00:29:30.790 --> 00:29:33.850
I mean, there were these big moments, but I did not know.
我是说，确实有这些重大时刻，但我当时真的不知道。

682
00:29:33.850 --> 00:29:35.950
And I remember being like, oh my God!
我记得当时我的反应是，天哪！

683
00:29:36.090 --> 00:29:40.270
And I definitely don't think a lot of the cast members knew.
而且我肯定很多演员当时都不知道。

684
00:29:40.630 --> 00:29:40.680
No.
没有。

685
00:29:40.680 --> 00:29:42.670
Because there were real reactions there.
因为那里的反应都是真实的。

686
00:29:42.890 --> 00:29:43.350
Yes.
是的。

687
00:29:43.830 --> 00:29:49.090
I also, I know we're going back a little bit, but I love that Kevin says he has to delete a lot.
我还想说，我知道这有点往回说了，但我很喜欢凯文说他必须删除很多内容。

688
00:29:49.430 --> 00:29:50.090
A lot.
很多。

689
00:29:50.390 --> 00:29:51.330
Gross, Kevin.
真恶心，凯文。

690
00:29:51.350 --> 00:29:52.950
What's going on over there?
那边在发生什么？

691
00:29:53.310 --> 00:29:55.170
Pam has a talking head next.
接下来是帕姆的采访片段。

692
00:29:55.390 --> 00:29:55.910
Oh, wait.
哦，等等。

693
00:29:56.070 --> 00:29:57.110
Can I say one thing?
我能说一件事吗？

694
00:29:57.110 --> 00:29:57.490
Yeah.
可以。

695
00:29:58.010 --> 00:30:01.830
Jenna, just to go back to Jim and Pam's conversation about Dwight and Angela.
珍娜，回到吉姆和帕姆关于德怀特和安吉拉的对话。

696
00:30:02.090 --> 00:30:02.290
Yeah.
嗯。

697
00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:04.610
This happens at 4 minutes, 45 seconds.
这发生在4分45秒处。

698
00:30:04.910 --> 00:30:06.970
I want you guys to rewatch the scene.
我想让你们重看这一幕。

699
00:30:07.630 --> 00:30:10.310
Pam is so grossed out.
帕姆感到非常恶心。

700
00:30:10.490 --> 00:30:11.390
And so is Jim.
吉姆也是。

701
00:30:11.570 --> 00:30:14.630
At the idea of Dwight and Angela, they're like, ugh.
一想到德怀特和安吉拉，他们就觉得，呃。

702
00:30:15.230 --> 00:30:16.970
I'm just like, come on.
我当时就想，拜托。

703
00:30:18.010 --> 00:30:18.970
What's wrong with that?
那有什么问题吗？

704
00:30:19.070 --> 00:30:20.530
Two people falling in love.
两个人坠入爱河而已。

705
00:30:20.690 --> 00:30:22.110
Pam is like, ugh, I can't.
帕姆就觉得，呃，我受不了。

706
00:30:22.710 --> 00:30:25.190
We are a little over the top about it.
我们对此确实有点反应过度了。

707
00:30:25.270 --> 00:30:26.150
You're so grossed out by it.
你对此感到非常恶心。

708
00:30:26.150 --> 00:30:27.410
I was like, jeez.
我当时就想，天哪。

709
00:30:28.370 --> 00:30:35.810
Well, Pam then goes and has a talking head where she says directly to the documentary film crew,
好吧，帕姆接着做了一个采访，她直接对着纪录片摄制组说，

710
00:30:35.990 --> 00:30:38.170
if you see anything, let me know.
如果你们看到了什么，一定要告诉我。

711
00:30:38.410 --> 00:30:38.930
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

712
00:30:38.990 --> 00:30:41.310
She's like all chummy with the documentary crew.
她跟纪录片摄制组混得挺熟的。

713
00:30:41.510 --> 00:30:43.070
She full on invites them to help.
她完全是在邀请他们帮忙。

714
00:30:43.070 --> 00:30:52.210
I think this is the first time we see this moment where someone in the show speaks directly to the character of the documentarian.
我想这是我们第一次看到剧中人物直接与纪录片拍摄者对话的时刻。

715
00:30:52.410 --> 00:30:52.630
Right.
没错。

716
00:30:52.750 --> 00:30:53.670
Who we never see.
虽然我们从未见过他们。

717
00:30:53.910 --> 00:30:54.250
Right.
没错。

718
00:30:54.430 --> 00:30:55.090
But, yeah.
但是，确实。

719
00:30:55.410 --> 00:30:55.690
Yeah.
是的。

720
00:30:55.770 --> 00:31:00.110
I think that Pam and Jim probably are the two people that engage with them the moSt.
我觉得帕姆和吉姆可能是跟他们互动最多的人。

721
00:31:00.210 --> 00:31:02.370
I mean, Michael, because he's a showboat, you know?
我是说，迈克尔也算，因为他爱出风头，你知道吧？

722
00:31:02.610 --> 00:31:04.370
But it's like Pam knows them.
但帕姆给人的感觉像是认识他们一样。

723
00:31:04.510 --> 00:31:05.750
That's what it felt like in that moment.
那一刻给人的感觉就是这样。

724
00:31:05.750 --> 00:31:05.990
Yeah.
没错。

725
00:31:06.110 --> 00:31:07.330
Like they're kind of friends or something.
就像他们是朋友什么的。

726
00:31:07.730 --> 00:31:08.290
All right.
好吧。

727
00:31:08.390 --> 00:31:10.210
So something else in Pam's talking head.
那么帕姆的采访里还有别的内容。

728
00:31:10.430 --> 00:31:14.510
At 4 minutes, 57 seconds, I'm tracking the mail cart now.
在4分57秒，我现在在追踪邮件推车。

729
00:31:14.750 --> 00:31:15.950
She is, you guys.
伙计们，她真的在追踪。

730
00:31:16.050 --> 00:31:17.510
She's become obsessed with the mail cart.
她对邮件推车着迷了。

731
00:31:17.710 --> 00:31:19.850
I'm tracking Casual Fridays and the mail cart.
我在追踪“休闲星期五”和邮件推车。

732
00:31:19.990 --> 00:31:24.530
And I want you all to know that Meredith comes over to the mail cart behind me during my talking head.
我想让你们都知道，在我接受采访时，梅雷迪思走到了我身后的邮件推车旁。

733
00:31:25.470 --> 00:31:26.050
Thank you.
谢谢。

734
00:31:26.050 --> 00:31:28.170
I'm applauding Jonah's mail cart tracking.
我为乔纳追踪邮件推车的行为鼓掌。

735
00:31:28.350 --> 00:31:29.430
The mail cart got used.
邮件推车被用上了。

736
00:31:30.250 --> 00:31:35.210
And then at 5 minutes, 12 seconds, there's just this interaction between Pam and Dwight that I love.
然后在5分12秒，帕姆和德怀特之间有一段互动，我非常喜欢。

737
00:31:35.310 --> 00:31:37.230
I actually love Pam and Dwight scenes.
我其实很喜欢帕姆和德怀特的对手戏。

738
00:31:37.470 --> 00:31:38.630
They're some of my favorite.
那是我最喜欢的场景之一。

739
00:31:38.990 --> 00:31:39.130
Yeah.
没错。

740
00:31:39.270 --> 00:31:42.810
You are often so, like, just exasperated by him.
你经常表现得对他非常恼火。

741
00:31:42.930 --> 00:31:45.270
And it's one of my favorite things you do as Pam.
这是你饰演帕姆时我最喜欢的表演之一。

742
00:31:45.590 --> 00:31:46.730
She comes up to him.
她走到他面前。

743
00:31:46.910 --> 00:31:47.810
Pam's on the case.
帕姆开始调查了。

744
00:31:47.930 --> 00:31:48.870
She's very excited.
她非常兴奋。

745
00:31:49.150 --> 00:31:49.950
Detective Pam.
侦探帕姆。

746
00:31:50.130 --> 00:31:53.970
She's like, Dwight, so my friend is kind of, you know, into these two girls.
她说，德怀特，我有个朋友，你知道的，他对这两个女孩有点意思。

747
00:31:54.130 --> 00:31:55.290
And Dwight's like, nice.
德怀特说，不错。

748
00:31:55.290 --> 00:31:57.830
And your face is like, oh, God.
而你的表情就像是，哦，天哪。

749
00:31:58.830 --> 00:32:05.110
At 5 minutes, 41 seconds, we find out that Dwight, as a volunteer sheriff, goes through everyone's medical records.
在5分41秒，我们发现德怀特作为志愿警长，会去翻看每个人的医疗记录。

750
00:32:05.290 --> 00:32:06.710
So that's great.
这真是太棒了。

751
00:32:07.010 --> 00:32:08.490
Gross, Dwight.
真恶心，德怀特。

752
00:32:08.770 --> 00:32:09.470
My gosh.
天哪。

753
00:32:09.990 --> 00:32:12.150
All right, Jenna, I have a thing that I track, you know.
好吧，珍娜，我有个追踪的小项目，你知道的。

754
00:32:12.270 --> 00:32:13.310
It's called old tech.
叫作“旧科技”。

755
00:32:13.530 --> 00:32:13.970
Oh, yeah.
哦，是吗。

756
00:32:14.010 --> 00:32:15.110
What's your old tech track?
你的“旧科技”追踪是什么？

757
00:32:15.270 --> 00:32:18.250
Guys, I think we should just call this the We Tracked It episode.
伙计们，我觉得我们应该把这集直接叫作“我们追踪到了”。

758
00:32:18.570 --> 00:32:19.530
We tracked it.
我们追踪到了。

759
00:32:19.530 --> 00:32:20.090
We're on the case.
我们正在调查。

760
00:32:20.170 --> 00:32:20.950
We're on the case.
我们正在调查。

761
00:32:21.210 --> 00:32:22.610
Much like Pam, we're on the case.
就像帕姆一样，我们正在调查。

762
00:32:22.730 --> 00:32:24.030
I love me some old tech.
我超爱旧科技。

763
00:32:24.030 --> 00:32:27.850
And at 5 minutes, 57 seconds, you see the Evite.
在5分57秒的时候，你看到了那个Evite邀请函。

764
00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:30.550
And you see, it's like so outdated looking.
你看，它看起来太老派了。

765
00:32:30.710 --> 00:32:36.710
If you go to Evite now, it's like, it looks like the old Evites of that day and age, if you will.
如果你现在去Evite网站，它看起来就像是那个年代的旧版邀请函，如果你懂我的意思的话。

766
00:32:36.710 --> 00:32:44.750
This is the scene where Michael is discovering the Evite, and he learns that Jim is having a barbecue at his house, and he is not invited.
这一幕是迈克尔发现Evite邀请函，得知吉姆在家里办烧烤派对，而他没被邀请。

767
00:32:44.930 --> 00:32:45.390
He's not invited.
他没被邀请。

768
00:32:45.490 --> 00:32:47.590
He sees the list of people who are invited.
他看到了受邀名单。

769
00:32:47.910 --> 00:32:49.810
And he is sort of looking around.
他还在四处查看。

770
00:32:49.810 --> 00:32:51.230
He's using his mouse, right?
他在用鼠标点，对吧？

771
00:32:51.410 --> 00:32:51.630
Yeah.
是的。

772
00:32:51.630 --> 00:32:53.990
And it all is so old looking.
而且一切看起来都太老了。

773
00:32:54.170 --> 00:32:55.070
Super old graphic.
超级古老的图形界面。

774
