00:39:10.250 --> 00:39:12.270
I didn't get through any line in that scene.
那一幕里我根本没法顺利说出任何台词。

928
00:39:12.450 --> 00:39:17.810
That line would be so hard for me to say, because it's coming off of him being so ridiculous.
那句台词对我来说太难说了，因为他当时表现得太荒唐了。

929
00:39:18.370 --> 00:39:21.190
Also, the whole time he's eating those dang noodles.
而且他全程都在吃那些该死的面条。

930
00:39:21.510 --> 00:39:21.830
Ugh.
呃。

931
00:39:22.070 --> 00:39:25.430
So I just, it was, I have to go back.
所以我当时，就是，我得回去看看。

932
00:39:25.490 --> 00:39:26.430
I want to watch the deleted.
我想看删减片段。

933
00:39:26.770 --> 00:39:27.650
Well, what is it?
嗯，是什么？

934
00:39:27.710 --> 00:39:28.210
The bloopers.
NG片段。

935
00:39:28.510 --> 00:39:29.590
You got to watch the bloopers.
你一定要看NG片段。

936
00:39:29.870 --> 00:39:34.310
At 8 minutes, 2 seconds, you guys, we find out what Jim thinks are the three ingredients
在8分02秒的时候，伙计们，我们知道了吉姆认为举办一场精彩派对的三个要素。

937
00:39:34.310 --> 00:39:35.870
for a great party.
第一，三箱进口啤酒。

938
00:39:35.870 --> 00:39:38.750
Hey, number one, three cases of imported beer.
第二，卡拉OK机。

939
00:39:38.970 --> 00:39:40.470
Number two, karaoke machine.
第三，别邀请迈克尔。

940
00:39:40.630 --> 00:39:42.130
Number three, do not invite Michael.
没错。

941
00:39:42.410 --> 00:39:42.590
Yeah.
我是说，他大概没说错。

942
00:39:43.790 --> 00:39:45.730
I mean, he's probably not wrong.
好吧。

943
00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:48.380
All right.
在8分25秒的时候，摄影组帮了帕姆一把。

944
00:39:48.460 --> 00:39:52.180
At 8 minutes, 25 seconds, the camera crew helps Pam.
我知道。

945
00:39:52.740 --> 00:39:53.480
I know.
摄像机冲向她的办公桌，示意她看向德怀特，她发现

946
00:39:53.480 --> 00:39:58.920
The camera rushes over to her desk and indicates that she should look over to Dwight, who she
德怀特正在吃那根安吉拉买的“宝贝露丝”巧克力棒。

947
00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:03.500
discovers is eating a baby Ruth bar, the one that Angela bought.
没错。

948
00:40:03.680 --> 00:40:04.240
That's right.
我记录的是你们俩串通一气。

949
00:40:04.380 --> 00:40:06.680
I have that you are in cahoots.
串通一气。

950
00:40:06.920 --> 00:40:07.660
In cahoots.
串通一气。

951
00:40:07.700 --> 00:40:10.160
Pam and the cameraman are in cahoots.
帕姆和摄影师串通一气。

952
00:40:10.320 --> 00:40:16.480
So first, Pam takes the step of talking directly to the camera crew, and now the camera crew has
首先，帕姆直接和摄制组对话，现在摄制组也

953
00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:17.580
gotten involved.
参与进来了。

954
00:40:17.880 --> 00:40:18.600
That's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

955
00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:22.660
No, I'm surprised that we did this so early in the series when I was watching this.
不，我惊讶的是，我在看剧时发现我们在剧集这么早期就做了这种安排。

956
00:40:22.780 --> 00:40:26.000
We're not that far in for us to be involving the crew like this.
我们还没进展到需要让摄制组这样参与进来的地步。

957
00:40:26.300 --> 00:40:29.560
People should know that our camera operator was Randall Einhorn.
大家应该知道，我们的摄影师是兰德尔·艾因霍恩。

958
00:40:29.780 --> 00:40:30.800
He's also our DP.
他也是我们的摄影指导。

959
00:40:31.060 --> 00:40:32.880
He went on to direct a bunch of episodes.
后来他还执导了许多集。

960
00:40:33.620 --> 00:40:37.840
And I had a really special relationship with Randall, and I remember filming the scene with
我和兰德尔有着非常特别的关系，我记得和他一起

961
00:40:37.840 --> 00:40:38.060
him.
拍摄那场戏的情景。

962
00:40:38.160 --> 00:40:40.400
He was really performing for me.
他当时真的在为我表演。

963
00:40:40.720 --> 00:40:45.720
He would come over, and he'd have a big smile on his face and a twinkle in his eye, and he
他会走过来，脸上带着灿烂的笑容，眼里闪烁着光芒，然后

964
00:40:45.720 --> 00:40:48.280
would motion over, he would give me a little thumbs up.
他会打手势，给我竖个大拇指。

965
00:40:48.400 --> 00:40:50.920
So all this interaction was happening.
所以当时有很多这样的互动。

966
00:40:51.020 --> 00:40:56.540
I felt like we were really performing together, and he was playing the character of the camera
我觉得我们真的在共同表演，他在扮演摄影师

967
00:40:56.540 --> 00:40:57.020
person.
这个角色。

968
00:40:57.300 --> 00:41:02.700
So I just have really fond memories of working with Randall in general when Pam would have
所以每当帕姆有非常感人的戏份时，我对和兰德尔合作的记忆

969
00:41:02.700 --> 00:41:04.500
really emotional scenes.
总是特别美好。

970
00:41:04.740 --> 00:41:07.480
Sometimes I would look at him, and he would be teared up.
有时我会看着他，发现他都热泪盈眶了。

971
00:41:07.480 --> 00:41:12.620
No, he's got a big heart, and he wears it on his sleeve, and we all got really attached
没错，他心肠很好，总是把感情写在脸上，我们大家都

972
00:41:12.620 --> 00:41:13.200
to Randall.
非常喜欢兰德尔。

973
00:41:13.440 --> 00:41:17.520
And I just think of him as sort of this very charming, blue-eyed Terminator.
我总觉得他就像是一个非常有魅力的蓝眼睛终结者。

974
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:18.380
Yeah.
没错。

975
00:41:18.600 --> 00:41:22.660
That's my—because you guys, you only ever see one of his eyeballs, because the other
这就是我的——因为你们，你们永远只能看到他的一只眼睛，因为另一只

976
00:41:22.660 --> 00:41:24.640
eyeball is looking through the lens.
眼睛正盯着镜头看。

977
00:41:24.640 --> 00:41:25.560
The little eyepiece.
那个小取景器。

978
00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:25.940
Yeah.
没错。

979
00:41:26.200 --> 00:41:32.160
So you see this one blue eye emoting emotion, and you're like, aw, you're like the friendly
所以你只能看到这只蓝眼睛在传达情感，你会觉得，噢，你就像个友好的

980
00:41:32.160 --> 00:41:32.780
Terminator.
终结者。

981
00:41:33.240 --> 00:41:34.680
The friendly Terminator.
友好的终结者。

982
00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:41.020
At 9 minutes, 29 seconds, you guys, oh, Jim, you just break my heart all the time.
在9分29秒的时候，天哪，吉姆，你总是让我心碎。

983
00:41:41.460 --> 00:41:42.900
But he's trying to be sly.
但他是在装傻。

984
00:41:43.080 --> 00:41:46.200
He's trying to do that thing where he figures out, is Roy going to come?
他想装作若无其事地打听，罗伊会来吗？

985
00:41:46.380 --> 00:41:47.520
But he's trying to play it cool.
但他想表现得酷一点。

986
00:41:47.620 --> 00:41:50.320
So he's like, yeah, I just, you know, I just need a head count.
所以他说，是啊，我只是，你知道，我只是需要统计一下人数。

987
00:41:50.720 --> 00:41:51.040
Yeah.
没错。

988
00:41:51.220 --> 00:41:52.600
Is Roy going to be there tonight?
罗伊今晚会去吗？

989
00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:53.540
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

990
00:41:53.580 --> 00:41:55.480
It's just because I need to know how many burgers to make.
只是因为我需要知道要做多少个汉堡。

991
00:41:55.640 --> 00:41:55.840
Yeah.
没错。

992
00:41:56.020 --> 00:41:57.180
I mean, this is the subtext, right?
我是说，这就是潜台词，对吧？

993
00:41:57.220 --> 00:41:57.800
It's nothing else.
没别的意思。

994
00:41:57.860 --> 00:42:01.400
It's not because I love you, and I want you to be in my apartment without your fiancé.
不是因为我爱你，想让你在没有未婚夫的情况下出现在我的公寓里。

995
00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:02.300
Yeah.
没错。

996
00:42:02.660 --> 00:42:04.220
Wait, is he—yeah, he's still your fiancé.
等等，他是——没错，他还是你的未婚夫。

997
00:42:04.220 --> 00:42:04.720
He is.
是的。

998
00:42:04.840 --> 00:42:05.180
I know.
我知道。

999
00:42:05.380 --> 00:42:06.460
It's hard to remember, right?
很难记住，对吧？

1000
00:42:07.060 --> 00:42:08.920
Fan question from Juan Martinez.
来自胡安·马丁内斯的粉丝提问。

1001
00:42:09.380 --> 00:42:14.720
Was Roy really unable to attend the party, or did Pam ditch him so she could hang out with Jim?
罗伊是真的没法参加派对，还是帕姆为了能和吉姆待在一起故意甩了他？

1002
00:42:14.980 --> 00:42:18.040
I don't think she ditched him, and I don't think she lied to him.
我觉得她没甩他，也没对他撒谎。

1003
00:42:18.340 --> 00:42:18.600
Yeah.
没错。

1004
00:42:19.040 --> 00:42:23.640
I think Pam was just as excited that Roy couldn't attend as Jim is.
我觉得帕姆和吉姆一样，对罗伊没法参加感到高兴。

1005
00:42:23.720 --> 00:42:26.000
Yeah, I think Roy probably has some dude hangout.
是啊，我觉得罗伊可能有什么哥们儿聚会。

1006
00:42:26.200 --> 00:42:28.300
He's very—he's kind of a dude dude, right?
他非常……他算是个挺大男子主义的人，对吧？

1007
00:42:28.840 --> 00:42:29.220
Yeah.
没错。

1008
00:42:29.220 --> 00:42:31.840
He probably has his thing, and also, Roy—
他可能有自己的事，而且，罗伊——

1009
00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:32.720
Roy wouldn't want to go.
罗伊根本不想去。

1010
00:42:32.820 --> 00:42:37.040
I was going to say, the last thing Roy wants to do is hang out with any of the Dunder Mifflin
我正想说，罗伊最不想做的事就是和邓德·米夫林公司的任何员工待在一起，

1011
00:42:37.040 --> 00:42:38.640
employees who's sort of over it.
那些对他来说已经过时的人。

1012
00:42:38.700 --> 00:42:40.700
They have to do enough of that probably for him.
他可能已经够受的了。

1013
00:42:41.020 --> 00:42:46.120
So he was, I think, happy to sit this one out, and Pam was like, oh, my God, oh, my God,
所以我认为，他很高兴能缺席这次活动，而帕姆当时心里肯定在想，天哪，天哪，

1014
00:42:46.180 --> 00:42:46.560
oh, my God.
天哪。

1015
00:42:46.600 --> 00:42:47.600
And so was Jim.
吉姆也是这么想的。

1016
00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:53.380
I'm, like, totally making this up, but maybe Pam waited kind of till the last minute to
我这完全是瞎猜的，但也许帕姆等到最后一刻才告诉罗伊关于派对的事，

1017
00:42:53.380 --> 00:42:57.140
tell Roy about the party so that it would be less likely that he could attend.
这样他能参加的可能性就更小了。

1018
00:42:57.320 --> 00:43:00.160
Like, I could see her maybe doing that.
我觉得她确实可能这么做。

1019
00:43:00.340 --> 00:43:03.220
And I could see her downplaying it, like, ugh, you know, I don't know.
我能想象她当时轻描淡写的样子，比如，哎呀，你知道的，我也不知道。

1020
00:43:03.300 --> 00:43:04.220
It's the thing I have to go to.
这就是我必须参加的活动。

1021
00:43:04.420 --> 00:43:05.060
Everyone's going.
每个人都要去。

1022
00:43:06.240 --> 00:43:06.880
Yes, 100%.
没错，百分之百。

1023
00:43:07.260 --> 00:43:08.200
It's going to be lame.
这会很无聊的。

1024
00:43:08.320 --> 00:43:08.780
You know what?
你知道吗？

1025
00:43:08.780 --> 00:43:09.980
If you don't want to go, you don't have to.
如果你不想去，你不必非得去。

1026
00:43:10.140 --> 00:43:10.740
Yeah, it's fine.
没关系，没事的。

1027
00:43:10.740 --> 00:43:15.420
I'll go because I feel like I have to, but I don't want you to have to change your plans.
我会去是因为我觉得我必须去，但我不想让你为了我改变计划。

1028
00:43:15.540 --> 00:43:16.120
I totally get it.
我完全理解。

1029
00:43:16.180 --> 00:43:17.200
If you don't want to go, it's okay.
如果你不想去，没关系的。

1030
00:43:17.600 --> 00:43:19.660
That's 100% how that went down, I believe.
我相信当时的情况百分之百就是这样发生的。

1031
00:43:20.040 --> 00:43:20.440
Yes.
没错。

1032
00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:21.460
All right.
好吧。

1033
00:43:21.600 --> 00:43:25.940
So now everyone's trying to get out of the office, and they're trying to avoid Michael
现在每个人都想离开办公室，他们都在躲着迈克尔，

1034
00:43:25.940 --> 00:43:28.540
because they all know he's not invited.
因为他们都知道他没被邀请。

1035
00:43:28.700 --> 00:43:32.700
So people are making up excuses to not hang out with him that night.
所以大家都在编借口，好在那天晚上不用和他待在一起。

1036
00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.680
And Angela, you have a great one.
安吉拉，你那个借口太棒了。

1037
00:43:34.940 --> 00:43:37.840
You say, charity, bake, drive.
你说的是：慈善、烘焙、义卖。

1038
00:43:38.440 --> 00:43:39.020
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1039
00:43:39.100 --> 00:43:39.380
I'm sure.
我敢肯定。

1040
00:43:39.460 --> 00:43:41.080
My character's, like, horrible at lying.
我的角色撒谎水平特别烂。

1041
00:43:41.200 --> 00:43:41.560
Horrible.
烂透了。

1042
00:43:41.800 --> 00:43:45.640
Well, a lot of people wrote in to ask if our excuses were scripted or improvised.
嗯，很多人写信来问我们的借口是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的。

1043
00:43:45.640 --> 00:43:47.960
Angela, was yours scripted or improvised?
安吉拉，你的那个是剧本写的还是即兴的？

1044
00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:49.020
Mine is a combo.
我的是结合体。

1045
00:43:49.300 --> 00:43:52.480
So my scripted line was charity, bake, drive.
剧本里的台词是：慈善、烘焙、义卖。

1046
00:43:52.680 --> 00:43:54.800
And then Michael's scripted line was liar.
然后迈克尔剧本里的台词是：骗子。

1047
00:43:55.180 --> 00:43:59.200
And then Steve improvised, you are a liar.
接着史蒂夫即兴发挥说：你是个骗子。

1048
00:43:59.420 --> 00:44:02.620
And then I improvised, no, I'm not, as I left.
然后我即兴回了一句：不，我不是，说完就走了。

1049
00:44:03.260 --> 00:44:04.860
And I didn't even look back.
我甚至头都没回。

1050
00:44:05.060 --> 00:44:06.120
And it stayed in.
这段被保留在了正片里。

1051
00:44:06.200 --> 00:44:09.800
And I think it's great because that's exactly how my character, I think, would have responded.
我觉得这很棒，因为我觉得这正是我的角色会有的反应。

1052
00:44:09.980 --> 00:44:10.260
Yes.
是的。

1053
00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:13.680
I just love that Dwight says he has soccer and clarinet practice.
我特别喜欢德怀特说他有足球和单簧管练习。

1054
00:44:14.480 --> 00:44:14.900
Yes.
是的。

1055
00:44:15.340 --> 00:44:16.180
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1056
00:44:16.240 --> 00:44:19.440
I feel like sometimes, I mean, you know, we have young children.
我觉得有时候，我是说，你知道，我们有年幼的孩子。

1057
00:44:19.440 --> 00:44:24.500
And sometimes when they're bad at lying, they just sort of list what their activities are.
有时候当他们不擅长撒谎时，他们就会列举出自己要参加的活动。

1058
00:44:24.500 --> 00:44:31.840
So I sort of feel like Dwight probably growing up had clarinet and soccer practice and he just went to default.
所以我感觉德怀特小时候可能真的有单簧管和足球练习，所以他只是习惯性地脱口而出。

1059
00:44:32.260 --> 00:44:37.220
Also, as Dwight leaves, he says, see you Monday, Michael.
另外，德怀特离开时说，周一见，迈克尔。

1060
00:44:37.600 --> 00:44:40.220
Casual Friday tracker coming at you.
休闲星期五追踪器向你走来。

1061
00:44:40.360 --> 00:44:41.500
No one's dressed casual.
没人穿得休闲。

1062
00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:42.180
No.
没有。

1063
00:44:42.400 --> 00:44:45.000
It's clearly a Friday because he says, see you Monday.
这显然是周五，因为他说周一见。

1064
00:44:45.700 --> 00:44:49.820
None of us are dressed casually, even though we're going to a barbecue after work.
我们没人穿得休闲，尽管我们下班后要去参加烧烤聚会。

1065
00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:51.760
Well, people are going to change clothes.
嗯，大家会换衣服的。

1066
00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:53.700
Don't you think they're going to go home and freshen up?
你不觉得他们会回家梳洗一下吗？

1067
00:44:53.700 --> 00:44:54.360
I don't want to.
我不想。

1068
00:44:54.540 --> 00:44:57.060
Listen, it's still not casual Friday.
听着，这依然不是休闲星期五。

1069
00:44:57.320 --> 00:44:57.980
I get it.
我明白。

1070
00:44:58.080 --> 00:44:58.480
I get it.
我明白。

1071
00:44:58.660 --> 00:45:01.920
We still set up in a previous episode that we have casual Fridays.
我们在之前的剧集里设定过我们有休闲星期五。

1072
00:45:02.160 --> 00:45:04.920
And yet here it is, a Friday, and none of us are dressed casually.
然而现在是周五，我们却没人穿得休闲。

1073
00:45:05.020 --> 00:45:05.580
No, you're right.
不，你说得对。

1074
00:45:05.660 --> 00:45:06.040
You're right.
你说得对。

1075
00:45:06.040 --> 00:45:07.180
I'm going to stay on this.
我会继续跟进这件事。

1076
00:45:07.280 --> 00:45:08.480
I think you stay on it.
我觉得你应该跟进。

1077
00:45:08.480 --> 00:45:09.280
Don't worry, everybody.
大家别担心。

1078
00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:10.720
I'm on it.
我在跟进。

1079
00:45:11.120 --> 00:45:12.320
I'm on the mail cart.
我在追踪邮件推车。

1080
00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:14.220
I'm on casual Friday.
我在追踪休闲星期五。

1081
00:45:14.500 --> 00:45:16.860
